{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Cutting {\n\n    private static int[] parseLineToIntArray(String line) {\n        return Arrays.stream(line.trim().split(\"\\\\s+\"))\n                     .mapToInt(Integer::parseInt)\n                     .toArray();\n    }\n\n    private static boolean hasEqualEvenOdd(int[] data, int pos) {\n        int even = 0, odd = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= pos; i++) {\n            if (data[i] % 2 == 0) even++;\n            else odd++;\n        }\n        return even == odd;\n    }\n\n    private static int findBestCutIndex(int[] arr, int budget, Set<Integer> forbidden) {\n        int best = -1;\n        int minDiff = budget + 1;\n\n        for (int i = 1; i < arr.length - 1; i++) {\n            int diff = Math.abs(arr[i] - arr[i + 1]);\n            if (diff < minDiff && hasEqualEvenOdd(arr, i) && !forbidden.contains(i)) {\n                minDiff = diff;\n                best = i;\n            }\n        }\n        return best;\n    }\n\n    public int maximizeCuts(int n, int money, int[] sequence) {\n        int remaining = money;\n        int count = 0;\n        Set<Integer> taken = new HashSet<>();\n\n        while (remaining > 0) {\n            int idx = findBestCutIndex(sequence, remaining, taken);\n            if (idx == -1) break;\n\n            taken.add(idx);\n            remaining -= Math.abs(sequence[idx] - sequence[idx + 1]);\n            count++;\n        }\n        return count;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n\n        int[] params = parseLineToIntArray(in.readLine());\n        int[] values = parseLineToIntArray(in.readLine());\n\n        Cutting solver = new Cutting();\n        int result = solver.maximizeCuts(params[0], params[1], values);\n\n        out.println(result);\n        out.flush();\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <set>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <sstream>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nvector<int> parseLineToIntArray(const string& line) {\n    vector<int> result;\n    istringstream iss(line);\n    int num;\n    while (iss >> num) {\n        result.push_back(num);\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nbool hasEqualEvenOdd(const vector<int>& data, int pos) {\n    int even = 0, odd = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= pos; i++) {\n        if (data[i] % 2 == 0) even++;\n        else odd++;\n    }\n    return even == odd;\n}\n\nint findBestCutIndex(const vector<int>& arr, int budget, const set<int>& forbidden) {\n    int best = -1;\n    int minDiff = budget + 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < (int)arr.size() - 1; i++) {\n        int diff = abs(arr[i] - arr[i + 1]);\n        if (diff < minDiff && hasEqualEvenOdd(arr, i) && forbidden.find(i) == forbidden.end()) {\n            minDiff = diff;\n            best = i;\n        }\n    }\n    return best;\n}\n\nclass Cutting {\npublic:\n    int maximizeCuts(int n, int money, vector<int> sequence) {\n        int remaining = money;\n        int count = 0;\n        set<int> taken;\n\n        while (remaining > 0) {\n            int idx = findBestCutIndex(sequence, remaining, taken);\n            if (idx == -1) break;\n\n            taken.insert(idx);\n            remaining -= abs(sequence[idx] - sequence[idx + 1]);\n            count++;\n        }\n        return count;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    string line;\n    getline(cin, line);\n    vector<int> params = parseLineToIntArray(line);\n    \n    getline(cin, line);\n    vector<int> values = parseLineToIntArray(line);\n\n    Cutting solver;\n    int result = solver.maximizeCuts(params[0], params[1], values);\n\n    cout << result << endl;\n\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.97731985989958e-05, -2.264974000354414e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0005421360838226974, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -5.960446742392378e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.622600959512056e-06, -0.006294781342148781, -8.344646857949556e-07, -3.0874729418428615e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.1787249594926834, -4.768370445162873e-07, -5.602820692729438e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.78448885679245, -1.311301275563892e-06, -9.536697689327411e-06, 0.0, -0.13645093142986298, -7.56950321374461e-05, -0.00023112009512260556, 0.0, -0.26510366797447205, -0.3868791162967682, -0.3417190611362457, -1.0490362910786644e-05, -2.264974000354414e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.11412239074707031, -1.311301275563892e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -4.291525328881107e-06, -7.033323527139146e-06, -4.768360213347478e-06, -5.972207145532593e-05, -0.023248590528964996, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -5.352353764465079e-05, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.001683605252765119, -5.841237907